# academics-agents

This repository is a Canvas-backed academic command centre. Before doing anything
school-related in this workspace, read `SKILL.md` in full — it is the operating
contract, and this file only carries the parts that must never be missed.

## The two rules that cost marks when broken

1. **Never state a deadline from memory.** Run `python3 scripts/refresh.py`, then
   `python3 scripts/dashboard.py`. Dates move, and a moved date is the failure
   mode that costs points. A remembered date is a guess wearing a number.

2. **Never invent a fact about a course.** If a source is silent, write
   `UNKNOWN — not stated in <file>` and name the file you checked. A marked gap is
   useful. A confident guess is worse than nothing.

## Reporting

State explicitly which courses the dashboard cannot see — a course with no Canvas
shell, or one that has published nothing. A clean report that quietly omits them
reads as "nothing is due" when the truth is "nothing is visible", and those are
very different weeks.

## Scope

Supports learning: deadline tracking, organising material, study guides, practice
problems, working past exams, checking a draft against the rubric, and drafting
messages to instructors.

Does not style generated work to read as hand-produced, and does not move material
past exam-lockdown controls.

**Nothing in this repo submits anything.** There is no submit function and that is
deliberate — submission is the student's action. Do not build one.

The instructor's stated policy overrides everything here, and those policies are
usually split by assessment type (permitted on a project, forbidden on a quiz).
Quote the policy verbatim in the course context and follow the split.

## Running things

The scripts read `.env` themselves. Nothing needs sourcing or exporting. Every
step is idempotent, so if one fails, fix it and re-run rather than working around
it.

| Script | What it does |
|---|---|
| `scripts/init.py` | asks for the Canvas address and token, verifies it, writes `.env` |
| `scripts/setup.py` | discover, scaffold, harvest, baseline, dashboard |
| `scripts/refresh.py` | re-pull and diff, leading with moved due dates |
| `scripts/dashboard.py` | grades, overdue, upcoming, and what it cannot see |

Never read, echo, or copy the contents of `.env`. It holds a live Canvas token.
